            <ArticleTitle>Prescribing policies of opioids for chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prescription of opioids often poses a difficult problem for the practitioner, particularly when they are confronted with institutionalised fears and restrictive regulations. This article compares prescribing policies for opioids in three European countries, Austria, Israel and Portugal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
